1
00:04:16,363 --> 00:04:22,363
Discover the adventure behind the greatest mystery of our time.

2
00:08:32,727 --> 00:08:38,727
Anastasia is a animation, family, fantasy film directed by Don Bluth.

3
00:12:49,090 --> 00:12:55,090
Ten years after she was separated from her family, an eighteen-year-old orphan with vague
memories of the past sets out to Paris in hopes of reuniting with her grandmother.

4
00:17:05,454 --> 00:17:11,454
She is accompanied by two con men, who intend to pass her off as the
Grand Duchess Anastasia to the Dowager Empress for a reward.

5
00:21:21,818 --> 00:21:27,818
Anastasia (voice), played by Meg Ryan.

6
00:25:38,181 --> 00:25:44,181
Dimitri (voice), played by John Cusack.

7
00:29:54,545 --> 00:30:00,545
Vladimir (voice), played by Kelsey Grammer.

8
00:34:10,909 --> 00:34:16,909
Rasputin (voice), played by Christopher Lloyd.

9
00:38:27,272 --> 00:38:33,272
Bartok (voice), played by Hank Azaria.

10
00:42:43,636 --> 00:42:49,636
Sophie (voice), played by Bernadette Peters.

11
00:47:00,000 --> 00:47:06,000
Anastasia is a 1997 American animated musical historical fantasy film directed and produced by Don Bluth and Gary Goldman from a screenplay by the
writing teams of Susan Gauthier and Bruce Graham, and Bob Tzudiker and Noni White, and based on a story adaptation by Eric Tuchman.

12
00:51:16,363 --> 00:51:22,363
It features songs written by Stephen Flaherty and Lynn Ahrens and a
musical score composed and conducted by David Newman.

13
00:55:32,727 --> 00:55:38,727
The film stars the voices of Meg Ryan, John Cusack, Kelsey Grammer, Christopher Lloyd,
Hank Azaria, Bernadette Peters, Kirsten Dunst, and Angela Lansbury.

14
00:59:49,090 --> 00:59:55,090
Set in an alternate 1926, it follows an amnesiac Anastasia
Romanov who embarks on a journey to discover her past.

15
01:04:05,454 --> 01:04:11,454
Anastasia was the first 20th Century Fox animated feature to be produced by its own animation
division, 20th Century Fox Animation, through its subsidiary Fox Animation Studios.

16
01:08:21,818 --> 01:08:27,818
The film premiered at the Ziegfeld Theater in New York City on November 14,
1997, and was released in the United States on November 21.

17
01:12:38,181 --> 01:12:44,181
The film received generally positive reviews from critics, who praised the animation, voice performances, and soundtrack,
though it attracted criticism from some historians for its fantastical retelling of the Grand Duchess.

18
01:16:54,545 --> 01:17:00,545
Anastasia grossed $140 million worldwide, making it the most
profitable film from Bluth and Fox Animation Studios.

19
01:21:10,909 --> 01:21:16,909
It received nominations for several awards, including for Best Original Song ("Journey to the
Past") and Best Original Musical or Comedy Score at the 70th Academy Awards.

20
01:25:27,272 --> 01:25:33,272
The success of Anastasia spawned a franchise, including a direct-to-video
spin-off in 1999 and a stage musical adaptation in 2016.

21
01:29:43,636 --> 01:29:49,636
The film explores themes of nightmare, villain, czar /
tsar / tzar, musical, based on true story.
